## PHẦN XI: TOKEN OPTIMIZATION

### XI.1 Context Loading Strategy

> **Rule:** Load only what you need, nothing more.

```yaml
context_tiers:

  TIER_1_HOT:
    priority: 1
    content: Session context, recent changes
    ttl: Current session
    size_limit: ~10KB
    
  TIER_2_WARM:
    priority: 2
    content: Project patterns, tech stack
    ttl: Until project changes
    size_limit: ~50KB
    
  TIER_3_COLD:
    priority: 3
    content: Specific files, tests
    ttl: Per task
    size_limit: ~100KB per file
    
  TIER_4_EXTERNAL:
    priority: 4
    content: External docs, web search
    ttl: Per query
    cost: High (tokens)
```

### XI.2 Token Budget Per Task Type

```yaml
token_budget:

  SIMPLE_FIX:
    context: "~500-1K tokens"
    code_output: "~1-3K tokens"
    total: "~2-5K tokens"
    
  MEDIUM_FEATURE:
    context: "~3-10K tokens"
    code_output: "~5-15K tokens"
    total: "~10-30K tokens"
    
  COMPLEX_SYSTEM:
    context: "~15-30K tokens"
    code_output: "~20-50K tokens"
    total: "~40-80K tokens"
```

### XI.3 Token Saving Techniques

```yaml
techniques:

  technique_1_summarize:
    name: "Summarize before load"
    before: "Load entire file"
    after: "Load relevant lines + summary"
    saved: "~70% tokens"
    
  technique_2_incremental:
    name: "Incremental context"
    before: "Load all context upfront"
    after: "Load minimal, add as needed"
    saved: "~40% tokens"
    
  technique_3_reference:
    name: "Reference vs content"
    before: "Paste code in prompt"
    after: "Reference path + describe"
    saved: "~50% tokens"
    
  technique_4_batch:
    name: "Batch operations"
    before: "Sequential tool calls"
    after: "Batch + reuse context"
    saved: "~30% tokens"
```

### XI.4 Context Compression Rules

```yaml
compression_rules:

  code:
    keep:
      - Function signatures
      - Key logic (core algorithm)
      - Test assertions
      - Error handling
    remove:
      - Verbose comments
      - Boilerplate
      - Imports (can infer)
      - Dead code
      
  docs:
    keep:
      - Key decisions
      - Constraints
      - Patterns
      - API contracts
    remove:
      - Examples (regenerate if needed)
      - Verbose explanations
      
  rules:
    keep:
      - Gate names
      - Key checks
      - Pass/fail criteria
    remove:
      - Detailed explanations
      - Repetitive sections
```

